<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leander Starr Jameson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1853–1917</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir Starr Jameson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leander Starr Jameson was a Scottish doctor and associate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-rhodes">Cecil Rhodes</a> who served as administrator for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mashonaland">Mashonaland</a> and led the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele Kingdom</a> in 1893. In 1895–1896 he led the failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jameson-raid">Jameson Raid</a> on the South African Republic, which forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a>'s resignation. He later served as prime minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> from 1904 to 1908.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leander-starr-jameson.jpg" alt="Leander Starr Jameson" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ball · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SirLeanderStarrJameson.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
